# Contact form, over Gmail SMTP.
#
# The form is submitted to a Next Server Action, which validates the input and
# then hands the message to Gmail over SMTP with nodemailer. No third party
# sits between the form and the inbox, and the password never leaves the
# server: it authenticates the account, so a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable would be an
# open relay for anyone who reads the bundle.
#
# SMTP_PASSWORD is a Google App Password, not the account password. Generate
# one at https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords, which requires two-step
# verification to be enabled on the account.
#
# The destination address is not here: it is IDENTITY.email, in
# src/content/site.ts, so the form and the mailto link beside it cannot drift.
#
# With either of these unset the form still renders and validates, and tells
# the visitor to email directly instead of pretending to send.

SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASSWORD=
